{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M9oE3n4L6xucqsvEsrpwbw","type":"tool_result","content":"288\tYou are going to encounter other study material. Videos, blog posts, practice question sets, competing books, a colleague's notes from when they passed. Some of it is excellent. Here is how to check whether it describes your exam, in about fifteen seconds:\n289\t\n290\t**Count the domains.** If the material is organized around **five** domains, or carries a standalone chapter or section titled \"Cloud Native Observability\" presented as a domain in its own right, it was built for the retired blueprint. That doesn't make its facts wrong; a Pod worked the same way in 2024. But its *weighting* is wrong, which makes its emphasis wrong, which makes its practice sets wrong, which makes the picture it hands you of where the exam's mass sits wrong. Specifically, it will under-serve Application Delivery by roughly half.\n291\t\n292\tUse it for facts if you like. Don't use it to allocate your time."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c5981c1-1384-4bf9-beb2-b0ec6f162fb8","uuid":"5a80182c-3561-460b-a63f-117fe0e11154","timestamp":"2026-08-24T08:02:57.774Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-01-taking-departure.md","content":"You are going to encounter other study material. Videos, blog posts, practice question sets, competing books, a colleague's notes from when they passed. Some of it is excellent. Here is how to check whether it describes your exam, in about fifteen seconds:\n\n**Count the domains.** If the material is organized around **five** domains, or carries a standalone chapter or section titled \"Cloud Native Observability\" presented as a domain in its own right, it was built for the retired blueprint. That doesn't make its facts wrong; a Pod worked the same way in 2024. But its *weighting* is wrong, which makes its emphasis wrong, which makes its practice sets wrong, which makes the picture it hands you of where the exam's mass sits wrong. Specifically, it will under-serve Application Delivery by roughly half.\n\nUse it for facts if you like. Don't use it to allocate your time.","numLines":5,"startLine":288,"totalLines":592}}}
